ateRank":75,"winningTimeRank":46,"winningTimeRankDir":26,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 1991 Comrades Marathon was the 66th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.200 km. The race was held on Friday, 31 May. Conditions: Mild pleasant day. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nNick BESTER claimed the men's title in 05:40:53, ahead of Shaun MEIKLEJOHN (05:43:55) and Colin THOMAS (05:45:13). Frith VAN DER MERWE won the women's race in 06:08:19, followed by Heleen REECE (06:54:17).\n\nFrith VAN DER MERWE's 06:08:19 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 15,014 entries, 12,077 runners crossed the finish line (80.4% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 11,151 men and 926 women (7.7% female). The average finish time was 09:28:02.\n\nMedals awarded: 13 Gold, 1,122 Silver, 10,942 Bronze. 3,717 runners (30.8%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Tok KOTZE in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 1989, the field was 10.7% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 28% of the finishers, with 8,697 seniors (avg 09:23:33) and 3,380 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}